-- title:
--   Riemann–Roch bound for mod-3 weight-2m functions on X₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ with $3 \nmid N$ such that some prime $q$ divides $N$ with $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $3$. Let $m \geq 1$ and let $\iota$ be a finite index type. Let $G : \iota \to$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` be a family in the intermediate field of $K((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $K$ all the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,K\,d\,(\bar\jmath)$ for nonzero divisors $d \mid N$, where $\bar\jmath =$ `jqModC K` is the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image in $K$ of the power series $jNum$. Assume each $G_i$, viewed as a Laurent series, satisfies `IsModPFormFn K m`, i.e. $G_i^6\,\bar\jmath^{4m}(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath$, and $G_i^2\,\bar\jmath^{m}(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath^{-1}$. Assume further that the family $G$ is linearly independent over $K$. Then, as rational numbers, $$\#\iota \;\le\; (2m-1)\bigl(\mathrm{genusFormula}(N) - 1\bigr) + \lfloor m/2 \rfloor\,\nu_2(N) + \lfloor 2m/3 \rfloor\,\nu_3(N) + m\,\varepsilon_\infty(N),$$ where the floors are natural-number divisions, $\nu_2(N) = \#\{x \in \mathbb{Z}/N : x^2 + 1 = 0\}$, $\nu_3(N) = \#\{x \in \mathbb{Z}/N : x^2 + x + 1 = 0\}$, $\varepsilon_\infty(N) = \sum_{d \mid N} \varphi(\gcd(d, N/d))$, and $\mathrm{genusFormula}(N) = 1 + \psi(N)/12 - \nu_2(N)/4 - \nu_3(N)/3 - \varepsilon_\infty(N)/2$ with $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$.
--
--   The right-hand side is the classical dimension of $M_{2m}(\Gamma_0(N))$ expressed through the genus, elliptic point counts and cusp count of $X_0(N)$; the statement is the Riemann–Roch upper bound half of a dimension count, obtained by placing each $G_i$ in the Riemann–Roch space of the weight-$2m$ floor divisor on the curve attached to the full modular function field in characteristic $3$. It feeds the lifting statement [`ModPForms.exists_mem_modPMod_ofPowerSeries_eq_qexpOfWeight_of_isModPFormFn_of_isAlgClosed_of_charP_three`](thm.html#ModPForms.exists_mem_modPMod_ofPowerSeries_eq_qexpOfWeight_of_isModPFormFn_of_isAlgClosed_of_charP_three), which identifies such $G$ with reductions of $q$-expansions of characteristic-zero forms of weight $2m$.
